Let $M$ be the midpoint of $[BC].$ Let $T$ be the point of trisection of $[AD],$ so that $MT \perp AD.$

[asy]
unitsize(0.30 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, E, F, G, T;

A = (5.83,16.95584);
B = (0,0);
C = (10,0);
D = foot(B,A,C);
E = reflect(B,C)*D;
F = extension(A,D,E);
G = foot(A,F);
T = foot(D,E);

draw(A--B--C--cycle);
draw(D--G);
draw(A--T);

label("$A$", A, SE);
label("$B$", B, SW);
label("$C$", C, SE);
label("$D$", D, SW);
label("$E$", E, N);
label("$F$", F, W);
label("$G$", G, NE);
label("$T$", T, N);
[/asy]

Let the semi-perimeter be $s = \frac{a + b + c}{2}.$ Note that $s = \frac{24 + r}{2} = 12 + r,$ where $r$ is the radius of the incircle.

Using the coordinates, we have $AD = \sqrt{(10 - 5.83)^2 + (0 - 16.95584)^2} = 19,$ and $MD = \sqrt{10^2 + \left(16.95584/3\right)^2} = 13.$

Note that the area of triangle $ABD$ minus the area of triangle $ABD$ is the area of triangle $AMC.$

\[\frac{1}{2} \cdot 10 \cdot 16.95584 - \frac{1}{2} \cdot 5.83 \cdot 16.95584 = \frac{1}{2} \cdot 10 \cdot (12 + r) \cdot \sin(90^\circ)\]
\[\implies 5.83(16.95584 - r) = 58(12 + r).\]
\[\implies \frac{7597 - 5.83r}{5.83} = 696 + 58r.\]
\[\implies 7597 - 5.83r = 37586 + 3308r.\]
\[\implies 3313.17r = -30049.\]
\[\implies r = \frac{-30049}{3313.17}.\]

Since the area is $\frac{1}{2} \cdot 20 \cdot r,$ the area is $m \sqrt{n - 1}.$

After performing the calculations, we get $m + n = \boxed{4094}.$ The answer is: 4094
